# Kitchen Skills Challenge student flow

Do not change other games. Do not change `sessionId` (`kitchen-day:<taskId>:<actorId>:<sessionDate>`).

- Student Trim / Reuse / Portion post `SILENT_ACTIVITY` (same data payload as before). Tutor `wastePracticeReview` posts `SILENT_ACTIVITY` with `actors: [selectedStudentActorId]` (no `studentId` property). The tutor iframe stays open after submit.
- Student persistence reads `kitchenGroupInputSelf.activities` (`GET /api/me/activities`). Do not require `activity.actor.id === me.id`. Keep `kitchenGroupInput` for trainer/group.
- After a successful silent post, keep the entry in local session state immediately. Merge/dedupe when self activities later arrive.
- Flow: Portion success → `#/kitchen-day/trim`. Forward tabs wait for prerequisites; the student may go back inside an unfinished task and back to completed sections. From Reuse or the challenge summary the student may return to Trim to add another ingredient. A started Trim ingredient must be saved before going forward to Reuse. Reuse success → summary (no EXIT yet). **Finish challenge** is only on that summary when there is no unfinished work, and posts `{ type: 'EXIT' }` via `postKitchenSkillsChallengeExit` / `postGameBusExit`. Never `postMessage` EXIT from the UI.
- Recipe and Trim ingredient pickers are searchable comboboxes that list ordered options when opened; typing filters. Ingredient options come only from the saved Portion recipe. Gram fields sanitize at the input (digits, one decimal, no letters, no negatives). Students are not shown waste % or recipe Hävikki.
- Official GameBus protocol: [`docs/contracts/GAMEBUS.md`](docs/contracts/GAMEBUS.md).
